From 6dfcb029d9083da18f8dcdb58ef4c16e8dbdb3dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:01:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add dry-run, confirmation, full-wipe guard, retry, and
 owner/repo support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

All four mutating scripts (transfer, visibility, delete, archive) now
share a small safety-core module that adds:

- --dry-run: preview exactly what would happen, with zero API calls.
- Typed confirmation before delete/transfer/visibility changes (not
  archive, which is reversible), with the repo count baked into the
  required phrase.
- A full-wipe guard: refuses to run when the target list exactly
  matches all_repos.txt's full contents, unless --force-full is passed.
  This is the sharpest version of a gap the README already names (no
  confirmation/dry-run) — a copy-paste mistake between list files could
  previously act on every repository the token can reach.
- Retry with exponential backoff, but only for errors that look
  transient (5xx, secondary rate limit, connection resets); a
  definitive 404 still fails immediately.
- --owner-repo: list-file lines can be "owner/repo" instead of always
  assuming the configured owner, closing the "owner/repository values
  are not supported" limitation the README already names. Bare lines
  still work unchanged.
- --public / --unarchive flags replace the previous "edit the source
  file to toggle this" pattern for visibility and archive status.
- A real pass/fail summary line at the end of each run.

package.json's test script now runs a real test suite
(test-safety-core.js) against a mocked Octokit-shaped client instead of
the placeholder "no test specified" stub.

README updated throughout to document the new flags.
