+## Safety Flags
+
+All four mutating scripts (transfer, visibility, delete, archive) support the same flags:
+
+| Flag | Effect |
+| --- | --- |
+| `--dry-run` | Prints what each script *would* do, per repository, without calling any mutating GitHub API. |
+| `--force-full` | Required to proceed when the target list exactly matches every name in `all_repos.txt` — otherwise that run is refused, since it's far more often an accidental copy-paste than an intentional "act on everything" request. |
+| `--owner-repo` | Interprets a list-file line containing `/` as an explicit `owner/repo` pair instead of assuming the configured owner for every line. A bare line still defaults to the configured owner, so existing list files work unchanged. Useful for managing repositories across more than one account or org from a single list file. |
 
-The script checks each repository's current status and skips repositories already in the requested state. After each update, it pauses briefly to allow the change to propagate.
+Delete, transfer, and visibility additionally require typed confirmation before making any change (e.g. `Type "DELETE 7 REPOS" to confirm...`) — the exact repository count is baked into the required phrase. Archive/unarchive does not, since it's fully reversible.
 
 ## Behavior and Limitations
 
 - Repositories are processed sequentially.
 - A failure is logged and processing continues with the next repository.
-- List entries are interpreted relative to the configured owner; `owner/repository` values are not supported.
-- The scripts do not retry failed API requests or poll transfer status.
+- List entries default to the configured owner; pass `--owner-repo` to specify `owner/repository` per line instead.
+- Failed requests are retried with backoff when they look transient (HTTP 5xx, secondary rate limiting, connection resets); a definitive error such as 404 fails immediately instead of retrying. The scripts still do not poll transfer status.
 - The transfer script may remove GitHub's archived status because archived repositories must be unarchived before transfer. It does not restore that status after transfer.
 - The visibility script restores archived status only after a successful visibility update. An API failure after unarchiving may leave a repository unarchived.
 - Archived repositories are read-only until they are unarchived.
